-- title:
--   Horizontal primes at a special-fibre point as kernels of sections
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, with $M/p \neq 0$, and assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC` of $j$ lies in the level-one $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for level $\Gamma_M$, whose data include the integral model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over $\operatorname{Spec}(R\,p)$, a curve model `Meta` of the geometric function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an isomorphism `eeta` from `Meta.C` onto the base change of the integral model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and $\rho \colon R\,p \to A$ a ring map inducing the structure map $R\,p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O'$ be a discrete valuation domain with maps $\rho_{O'} \colon R\,p \to O'$, an injective local map $\iota_{A'} \colon O' \to A$ with $\iota_{A'} \circ \rho_{O'} = \rho$, and $j_{O'} \colon O' \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with $\rho_{O'}$ and equal to $\iota_{A'}$ followed by the inclusion of $A$, the residue maps being compatible as well. Let $x'$ be a point of the base change `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO'` of the integral model to $O'$ lying over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O'$, and $\varpi'$ a generator of the maximal ideal of $O'$. Write $XQ$ for the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\mathrm{prJ}'\colon XQ \to$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO'` for the map induced by $j_{O'}$, $B$ for the stalk at $x'$, and $\sigma_B \colon O' \to B$ for the composite of the global-sections map of the structure morphism with the germ at $x'$. The assertion is: for every nonzero prime ideal $P$ of $B$ with $\sigma_B(\varpi') \notin P$ there are a place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`IsRational`), and a morphism $s' \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO'` over $\operatorname{Spec}\iota_{A'}$, such that the restriction of $s'$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of `Meta.C` corresponding to $W$ under `Meta.pointEquivPlace`, followed by `eeta` and then $\mathrm{prJ}'$, and such that $s'$ sends the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to $x'$; and then $P$ is exactly the kernel of the ring map $\chi \colon B \to A$ obtained from the stalk identification along this specialisation followed by the map on local rings induced by $s'$ at the closed point.
--
--   This is the statement that a horizontal prime of the local ring of the Deligne–Rapoport model base-changed to $O'$ at a point of the special fibre is the centre of a rational place of the geometric function field, realised by an $A$-valued section through that point. It is the point-generic form of the stalk-reading step, and is used by the two lemmas identifying the image of the stalk in the function field under integrality hypotheses at strict first and second branches.
